Subject: [PATCH] [Kernel] K8V4 KV cache ops: FP8 keys + NVFP4 values (Triton
 writer, decode, prefill gather)

Triton kernels for a K8V4 KV cache (FP8 E4M3 keys, NVFP4 values with E4M3
block scales per 16 elements and a per-layer global scale), page planes
[K | V codes | V scales] per HND page. The writer reproduces the QW38
accuracy emulation's quantizers exactly; decode/verify runs BF16 math on
exactly dequantized K/V; the gather produces dense FP8 pages for the FP8
prefill FMHAs. Unit tests vs the emulation and an FP32 reference.

